   * @param connection
   * @param orderItemId The identifier of the order item that owns the cancellation request.
   * @param cancellationRequestId The identifier of the cancellation request to approve within the specified order item scope.
   * @x-autobe-authorization-type null
   * @x-autobe-authorization-actor seller
   * @x-autobe-specification Load the cancellation request by cancellationRequestId and verify it belongs to orderItemId before making any state changes. Reject the request with a not-found, forbidden, or conflict error if the association does not match, if the request is not pending, or if the order item is already in a final state that prevents cancellation.
   *
   * Perform the approval in a single transaction. Insert cancellation-request snapshot records according to the snapshot model so the pre-decision and post-decision state can be reconstructed later. Update the cancellation request with the approved outcome and any reviewer metadata required by the schema. If the order item has not yet reached a final outcome, change its status to cancelled and create an inventory record that restores the cancelled quantity for the related product variant. Trigger any refund-processing flow required by the cancellation approval policy.
